# ⚠ An agent worktree is a second checkout of this repository inside it. Committing one would
# duplicate every project and every corpus file; `Testing/corpus/real/NOTICE.md` records what
# sampling from one cost.
.claude/worktrees/

# Skala's own working directory: conformance reports and crash reproductions.
# ⚠ A crash artefact under .skala/crash/ is a bug report, not a build output — copy it into
# Testing/corpus/pathological/ deliberately rather than committing the whole directory.
.skala/
# doc 17's parity pipeline: generated inputs and outputs, re-made by a re-run.
# ⚠ `types-2026.xml` is NOT in this list any more, and its absence was a real defect rather
# than tidiness. It is a dumped snapshot of an external tool's catalogue, not a build output:
# it needs `jb inspectcode --dumpIssuesTypes`, ReSharper is being retired, and re-dumping it
# from a later release would silently change every parity number measured against it. While it
# was ignored, `verify_ledger.py`'s strongest assertion — that every `catalogued.json` key names
# a real inspection — did not run in any fresh clone or worktree, and the run still printed
# `0 failures` (#311). Committing the snapshot is what makes that check unskippable.
Testing/parity-analysis/types.json
Testing/parity-analysis/universe.json
Testing/parity-analysis/classified.json
Testing/parity-analysis/sonar.json
